{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/413242-hedge-and-it-s-relations-to-earth","id":413242,"title":"Hedge and it's relations to Earth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-20T15:37:56-08:00","id":413242,"title":"Hedge and it's relations to Earth","content":"I want to run a first Hedge journey for the players. But I really do not know that is time relation of Bramble to the Earth. I looked in 1ed corebook and <b>Rites of Spring</b> and could not find quickly answers on topics I asked here, so I hope for your help here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In Arcadia, we know time pass slower or faster than on the Mortal Realm. In Fairy three days can be three decades on Earth, or five years of Durance become five hours since the mortal was taken by the Gentry. <br /> <br /> But how this relations come to the Hedge, that is in &quot;half of way&quot; from both worlds? Is a time flows mostly in there like on Earth - and the full moon midnight of Thursday on New York is still full moon midnight of Thursday in the Brambles there? Or maybe there are difference in time - like an few hours missing, but not enough for character to spent here life there? In this scenario mortal can gone for Hedge at dusk, but awake in there at local dawn.<br /> <br /> What about seasons in Hedge? I know that powerful changelings in Wyrd leaves imprints of their Mien ( and Mantle ), so those from Seasonal Courts leave their seasons flow on the Bramble. Still, some general season should be in the local Hedge. If the spring on Earth is mirrored with green leaves and new beings stalking it's labirynth? Or maybe that when Autumn comes to Earth, the Hadge is still in the clutches of Summer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T16:20:35-08:00","id":413344,"title":"","content":"The way I see it is that the hedge spans the whole &quot;distance&quot; between Earth and Arcadia. Those parts &quot;closer&quot; to earth are more earth-like and rational while those &quot;further&quot; from earth are stranger and more fantastical. When you open a new gate you're likely to get somewhere &quot;close&quot; that reflects the mortal world where you opened the gate from. You'll need to travel some to get somewhere &quot;further&quot; from earth altho once you've found a far place you can install the hedge side of an existing gate to easy access.<br /> <br /> In the &quot;close&quot; hedge I have time follow the standard rules we know on Earth. 24 hours in a day with day and night as you're expect and the moon keeping the same phase when it's visible through the thorns. I rotate the seasons with the change in power of the local freehold, where applicable.<br /> <br /> When you get &quot;far&quot; from Earth then you start getting weird stuff like time distortion and seasons that don't exist in the human world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T16:33:03-08:00","id":413357,"title":"","content":"I'm with helel here. But I also think that the parts of the Hedge close to Earth (or Arcadia) are mostly the exception. So when you arrive in the Hedge you'll arrive near Earth; but you'll <b>very</b> quickly end up in the middle hedge unless you're explicitly doing something to ensure you stay near Earth. Examples would be: trying to navigate to New York, trying to navigate to a Hollow that's near Earth, staying on a Trod that's near Earth.<br /> <br /> Check out Dream Catchers for lots of hedge navigation goodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}